From: OpenWrt MR80X v2 port
Subject: mtd: spinand: esmt: do not register the OTP areas

Kernel 6.18 added OTP support for the ESMT F50L1G41LB and F50D1G41LB. On the
Mercusys MR80X v2 (IPQ5018, QPIC SPI NAND) registering those areas makes the
SPI NAND unusable, in two separate ways.

The first one has a proper fix elsewhere. qcom_spi_send_cmdaddr() used to run
the command before qcom_spi_io_op() wrote the value into NAND_FLASH_FEATURES,
so every SET_FEATURE landed one operation late. spinand_otp_rw() enables OTP
mode, reads, and disables it again, and mtd_otp_nvmem_add() does exactly that
during MTD registration, so the "disable" wrote the previously requested value
and CFG_OTP_ENABLE stayed set. The chip then serves its OTP area instead of the
array: page 0 returns the unique ID page, page 1 the ONFI parameter page,
everything above reads as 0xff. Reads report no error, because the hardware
erased-page detector legitimately flags those pages as blank, and writes fail
with -EIO. It looks exactly like a wiped flash while the content is untouched.

That off-by-one is fixed by "spi: spi-qpic-snand: write the feature value
before executing SET_FEATURE" from openwrt/openwrt#24197, which this tree also
carries. Measured here before that fix:

  cfg as found at probe = 00 (otp_en=0)   first probe, chip is clean
  cfg as found at probe = 40 (otp_en=1)   second probe, OTP was left on
  OTP off: cached=00 chip=40 -> chip=00   cache and chip disagree

The second one is why this patch is still needed. With the SET_FEATURE fix in
place and the OTP declarations restored, the spinand probe fails outright, four
milliseconds after the chip is identified:

  spi-nand spi0.0: ESMT SPI NAND was found.
  spi-nand spi0.0: 128 MiB, block size: 128 KiB, page size: 2048, OOB size: 64
  spi-nand spi0.0: probe with driver spi-nand failed with error -512

No MTD device is created at all, so there are no partitions, no calibration
data and no sysupgrade. It reproduces on a manual driver rebind, so it is not a
timing race. Dropping the OTP declarations makes it probe cleanly every time.
Why the registration returns -ERESTARTSYS on this board is not established; one
difference against the TP-Link Archer AX55 v1, which runs the same silicon with
OTP enabled, is that this device tree hangs an nvmem-layout off the 0:art
partition for the WiFi calibration data.

The feature is unused on this hardware and the rest of the chip support is
untouched. 6.12 is unaffected because it carries no OTP support for these parts.

The analysis above and the fix itself originate from the equivalent patch in
the Gameplayer-1-8/openwrt_mrx80_v2 tree (Mercusys MR80X v2, same IPQ5018 +
ESMT F50L1G41LB/F50D1G41LB silicon family). Carried here unmodified because
the Mercusys MR80X v5 hits the identical OTP registration bug on the same
chip family; confirmed independently on v5 hardware in this tree before this
patch was found, matching the same "cache and chip disagree" / probe failure
symptoms described above.

Signed-off-by: Fabiano Tassotti <fabianotassotti@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/esmt.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/esmt.c
@@ -208,9 +208,7 @@
 					      &write_cache_variants,
 					      &update_cache_variants),
 		     0,
-		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f50l1g41lb_ooblayout, NULL),
-		     SPINAND_USER_OTP_INFO(28, 2, &f50l1g41lb_user_otp_ops),
-		     SPINAND_FACT_OTP_INFO(2, 0, &f50l1g41lb_fact_otp_ops)),
+		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f50l1g41lb_ooblayout, NULL)),
 	SPINAND_INFO("F50D1G41LB",
 		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_ADDR, 0x11, 0x7f,
 				0x7f),
@@ -220,9 +218,7 @@
 					      &write_cache_variants,
 					      &update_cache_variants),
 		     0,
-		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f50l1g41lb_ooblayout, NULL),
-		     SPINAND_USER_OTP_INFO(28, 2, &f50l1g41lb_user_otp_ops),
-		     SPINAND_FACT_OTP_INFO(2, 0, &f50l1g41lb_fact_otp_ops)),
+		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f50l1g41lb_ooblayout, NULL)),
